# Written to ~/.zshrc.local by `chezmoi apply` the first time it runs, then
# never touched again — fill in per-machine secrets and paths here. zshrc
# sources this automatically if it exists, after PATH/mise/compinit and
# before the tool blocks that read these values.
#
# Mode 0600 already, from the source name's `private_` attribute.

# ── Secrets ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Model-provider keys are the exception to this file. Put ANTHROPIC_API_KEY and
# OPENAI_API_KEY in ~/.omp/agent/.env instead: omp loads that dotenv file
# itself, so the keys are present no matter how omp is launched, while this
# file only reaches processes started from a login shell.
#
# Setting the variable is also not sufficient on its own. A stored OAuth session
# outranks every environment variable in omp's credential order, so on a machine
# that has run `/login`, the key is ignored until it is pinned in
# ~/.omp/agent/models.yml. See omp/agent/models.yml.example.
# export GITHUB_PERSONAL_ACCESS_TOKEN='github_pat_...'
# export FIGMA_ACCESS_TOKEN='figd_...'
# export RUNPOD_API_KEY='rpa_...'
# export HF_TOKEN='hf_...'

# ── Work context ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# export AWS_PROFILE='...'
# export AWS_REGION='us-east-2'

# ── Machine-specific build flags ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# Each `brew --prefix` is a subprocess on every shell start — only add the
# ones you actually build against.
# export LDFLAGS="-L$(brew --prefix tcl-tk@8)/lib"
# export CPPFLAGS="-I$(brew --prefix tcl-tk@8)/include"
# export PKG_CONFIG_PATH="$(brew --prefix tcl-tk@8)/lib/pkgconfig"

# Apple Silicon: let unimplemented MPS ops fall back to CPU instead of erroring.
# export PYTORCH_ENABLE_MPS_FALLBACK=1
